d2d1: say once when a shaped layer mask engages the stencil

A smoke test where the new stencil path never executes and one where it executes
correctly produce identical-looking apps. Without a marker, "Premiere looks fine" is
not evidence that the path was exercised -- it is equally consistent with the path
never running, which is a much weaker result than it appears.

One ERR, once per process, naming the target size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -3325,6 +3325,15 @@
             && d2d_device_context_ensure_stencil(context))
     {
         unsigned int slot = context->layer_depth;
+        static LONG announced;
+
+        /* One line, once per process: a smoke test where this path never runs and one where it
+         * runs correctly look identical otherwise, and "looks fine" is not evidence that the new
+         * code was exercised. */
+        if (!InterlockedExchange(&announced, 1))
+            ERR("neutron-stencil: shaped layer mask engaged (target %ux%u) -- "
+                "masks now stencilled rather than clipped to their bounds\n",
+                context->pixel_size.width, context->pixel_size.height);
 
         d2d_device_context_stencil_mask(context, layer_parameters->geometricMask,
                 &layer_parameters->maskTransform, +1);
@@ -4532,6 +4541,15 @@
             && d2d_device_context_ensure_stencil(context))
     {
         unsigned int slot = context->layer_depth;
+        static LONG announced;
+
+        /* One line, once per process: a smoke test where this path never runs and one where it
+         * runs correctly look identical otherwise, and "looks fine" is not evidence that the new
+         * code was exercised. */
+        if (!InterlockedExchange(&announced, 1))
+            ERR("neutron-stencil: shaped layer mask engaged (target %ux%u) -- "
+                "masks now stencilled rather than clipped to their bounds\n",
+                context->pixel_size.width, context->pixel_size.height);
 
         d2d_device_context_stencil_mask(context, layer_parameters->geometricMask,
                 &layer_parameters->maskTransform, +1);
